<urn:atm:triage:finding/AV3-B6>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AV3-B6" ;
  triage:title "AV.3 read-handler gate parser defect: av3_handler_region joins multiple handler fns and av3_assert_allowlisted_types wraps the joined text as `fn gate() {region}`, which cannot parse for >1 handler" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr ruling msg 01M1BG9Z99RSCN9A322GVQSSZW (re-verified firsthand at c9b71d720): test av3_post_cutover_read_handlers_reject_legacy_blocking_dependencies (crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs ~:3491) fails against AV.1b — a pure parser defect that never reaches allowlist logic. av3_handler_region (~:3977) concatenates several handler function bodies and av3_assert_allowlisted_types (~:3991-3992) wraps the joined text in `fn gate() {region}` then syn::parse_file — unparseable for more than one handler. The gate could never parse the plural handler set its own read_handler_names() (~:4110) requires; it only ever passed because the AsyncMailboxRuntime activation marker kept it dormant. Latent AV.3 defect exposed by AV.1b activation, not an AV.1b regression." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-av" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "tooling" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-31T09:36:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
